{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/54851-cwod-suggested-books-and-films","id":54851,"title":"CWOD: Suggested Books and Films","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-21T13:05:56-08:00","id":54851,"title":"CWOD: Suggested Books and Films","content":"Every Corebook or sometimes, Player's Guides and other sourcebooks would have a short section of books, film, shows, music albums, and even video games suggested for the mood of the game.<br /> <br /> So what do you think fits the mood of a certain setting? Seeing as there has been a huge gap worth of material for years now that the CWOD has come back with 20th editions.<br /> I'll submit a few to get the ball rolling.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse:</b><br /> Sharp Teeth by Toby Barlow (Book/Novel: Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers)<br /> <br /> <b>Mage: the Ascension:</b><br /> Detentionaire (Animated show, aired in Canada/Australia, but you can view it online. The show changes a lot from season one to season four: For games involving the Technocracy.)<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling: The Dreaming:</b><br /> Spirited Away (Animated Movie)<br /> The Cat Returns (Animated Movie)<br /> <br /> <b>General Classic World of Darkness:</b><br /> Gravity Falls (Animated show, it's more humorous, but there is a general set of unease in the atmosphere as well.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T23:59:02-08:00","id":55297,"title":"","content":"Hunter: the Reckoning:<br /> They Live (film) - Sudden awareness of enemies all around you that others can't see. Also heavily quotable, and the vector by which a phrase involving bubblegum and kicking ass entered cultural consciousness.<br /> Darker Than Black (Animated TV Series) - Not necessarily for any thematic reason, but the Contractors all have powers that work by incredibly idiosyncratic means that could be used as triggers. Hazuki Mina, who shows up later into the series, demonstrates a talent that's a dead ringer for Cleave (and also a bit of Impact).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T12:45:53-08:00","id":60056,"title":"","content":"Have some new stuff to add, some video games.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Changeling: the Dreaming:</b></u><br /> <b>The Secret of Monkey Island and The Secret of Monkey Island 2: LeChuck's Revenge.</b> (Computer/Video Games: The very first game was mentioned in passing in C:tD 2nd ed.'s Storytellers Guide book. But was not listed in any &quot;Suggestion lists&quot; after that. I think the second should count just for <i>that</i> ending. Both games have received an update in graphics thanks to the Special Editions, but I will always remember playing it on the Amiga when it first came out.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_RJKq-TX_ts\" data-code=\"_RJKq-TX_ts\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_RJKq-TX_ts/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <b>Puppeteer</b> (Video Game: Just recently heard word about this game for the PS3 and I ordered it. There's an unseelie Bear Pooka that's taken over an area in the Far/Deep Dreaming that reflects the Moon.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T07:07:32-08:00","id":829230,"title":"","co